nt status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRIC INDUSTRIAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NOMURA, TAKAIKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OGAWA, KAZUFUMI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OTAKE, TADASHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKEBE, TAKAKO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NOMURA TAKAIKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OGAWA KAZUFUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OTAKE TADASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKEBE TAKAKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NOMURA, TAKAIKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OGAWA, KAZUFUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OTAKE, TADASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKEBE, TAKAKO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method for preparation of a functional film derived from a silane type compound which is used for modifying the property of the surface of a substrate, characterized by comprising applying to a substrate a solution for an undercoating layer containing a hydrolyzable compound represented by X-(SiOX2)n-SiX3 wherein X is at least one compound selected from the group consisting of a halogen atom, an alkoxy group and an isocyanate group and n is an integer of 0 or more, drying the solution to thereby form an undercoating layer, applying a solution containing a silane type compound to the undercoating layer to render molecules of the silane type compound to be adsorbed thereon, and calcining the resultant substrate at a temperature of 300  DEG C or higher. The method can be used for providing a aforementioned functional film having improved water repellency, durability and resistance to water.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne un procédé de fabrication d'un film fonctionnel dérivé d'un composé de type silane qui est utilisé afin de modifier les propriétés de surface d'un substrat. Ce procédé se caractérise en ce que l'on applique sur un substrat une solution permettant de former une couche inférieure contenant un composant hydrolysable qui correspond à la formule X-(SiOX2)n-SiX3 où X représente au moins un composé choisi dans le groupe comprenant un atome halogène, un groupe alcoxy et un groupe isocyanate, tandis que n est un nombre entier de 0 ou plus. Ce procédé consiste ensuite à sécher la solution de manière à former la couche inférieure, à appliquer une solution contenant un composé de type silane sur la couche inférieure de manière que les molécules du composé de type silane soient absorbées par cette dernière, et à calciner le substrat obtenu à une température de 300  DEG C ou plus. Ce procédé peut être utilisé afin de produire un film fonctionnel tel que celui susmentionné, qui possède de meilleures caractéristiques hydrofuges, de durabilité et de résistance à l'eau.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>